message.content:
Below is a minimal example of a rotating card that turns 180 degrees around the Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to adjust the size, colors, or animation duration to fit your design.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
  /* Container that keeps the card centered */
  .card-wrapper {
    perspective: 1000px;          /* gives a 3D effect */
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    margin: 50px auto;
  }

  /* The card itself */
  .card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    background: #fff;
    border-radius: 12px;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* smooth rotation */
    transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* keep children in 3D space */
    position: relative;
  }

  /* Hover effect – rotate 180° around Y axis */
  .card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
  }

  /* Front side of the card */
  .card .front,
  .card .back {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;   /* hide backside when flipped */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: #333;
    padding: 20px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .card .front {
    background: #f9f9f9;
  }

  /* Back side – rotated 180° so it shows when card flips */
  .card .back {
    background: #e0e0e0;
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="front">
      <h2>Front Side</h2>
      <p>Hover over this card to see the flip effect.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="back">
      <h2>Back Side</h2>
      <p>This is the other side of the card.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works
1. **Perspective** – The `.card-wrapper` sets a perspective so the 3D rotation looks realistic.
2. **Transform-style** – `preserve-3d` keeps the child elements in 3D space.
3. **Backface visibility** – Hides the backside of each side when it’s not facing the viewer.
4. **Hover** – On hover, the card rotates 180° around the Y‑axis, revealing the back side.

You can replace the content inside `.front` and `.back` with images, icons, or any other HTML you need. Adjust the `transition` duration or the `transform` angle (e.g., `rotateY(360deg)` for a full spin) to customize the animation.
